              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="updateChannelActivityLog" id="0ea1fe53-089b-4bab-9d04-1d22c8b7f8d7">
                <documentation>Update details of logged record</documentation>
              </element>
            </folder>
            <folder name="Card Transaction Switch" id="ef36e769-573e-4bb5-ab62-a2aa3bfb015f">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Card Transaction Switch" id="89cf424b-074e-45ff-969e-6d5aee528111">
                <documentation>Example of use:
An authorization request or sale transaction message is received from the Point of Sale device by the Acquiring Bank, which then needs to route the message to the Card Issuing Bank through the Card Network (e.g. Visa, MC, AMEX or Diners etc.), await the response from the Card Issuer and communicate it to the Merchant through the Point of Sale device.

General comment:
This service domain handles the processing and asynchronous switching of Card Transaction related messages, such as Authorization, Sale, Void, Refund, etc. between the Acquiring Bank and the Issuing Bank through the Card Network. It has a role within the Acquiring Bank in switching transactions acquired from the Merchant to the Card Network, within the Card Network to switch the transaction to the applicable Card Issuer, and within the Card Issuer to switch the transaction to the instance of the Card Authorization service domain for the card product involved.

Business Purpose
Orchestrate the switching and routing of Card Authorization and Financial transactions received through the Card POS Network, Card E-Commerce Gateway, or the ATM Network from the Acquirer to the Issuer through the Card Networks.






Пример использования:
Запрос на авторизацию или сообщение о сделке продажи поступает из точки продажи устройства банком-эквайером, который затем должен направить сообщение в банк-эмитент карты через сеть карт (например, Visa, MC, AMEX или Diners и т.д.), дождитесь ответа от эмитента карты и передайте его продавцу через точку продажи устройства.

Общее замечание:
Этот домен обслуживания регулирует обрабатывать и асинхронное переключение сообщений карточки отнесенных Трудыами, как утверждение, сбывание, свободное пространство, возврат, etc. между банком-эквайером и Банком-эмитентом через сеть карт. Он играет важную роль в банк-эквайер в переключении операций, приобретенных от торговца к сети карточки, в карте сети для переключения операций применимому эмитента карты, и в карты эмитента для переключения сделки к экземпляру авторизации службы домена для карточки продукта.

деловая цель
: Организовывать переключение и маршрутизацию авторизации карт и финансовых транзакций, полученных через сеть POS карт, шлюз электронной коммерции карт или сеть банкоматов от эквайера к эмитенту через сети карт.


Service Domain - Card Transaction Switch
This service domain handles the processing and asynchronous switching of Card Transaction related messages, such as Authorization, Sale, Void, Refund, etc. between the Acquiring Bank and the Issuing Bank through the Card Network. It has a role within the Acquiring Bank in switching transactions acquired from the Merchant to the Card Network, within the Card Network to switch the transaction to the applicable Card Issuer, and within the Card Issuer to switch the transaction to the instance of the Card Authorization service domain for the card product involved

Executive Summary
This service domain orchestrates the switching and routing of Card Authorization and Financial transactions received through the Card POS Network, Card E-Commerce Gateway, or the ATM Network from the Acquirer to the Issuer through the Card Networks

Examples Of Use
An authorization request or sale transaction message is received from the POS device by the Acquiring Bank, which then needs to route the message to the Card Issuing Bank through the Card Network, await the response from the Card Issuer and communicate it to the Merchant through the POS device



</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="activateCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="98ac9175-67e8-4374-9400-e3fddaa4eb8c">
                <documentation>Assign responsibility for the card transaction switch operating session</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="configureCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="1f435903-20a0-453a-816b-fedd4ac068d2">
                <documentation>Amend the configuration arrangements/parameters governing the card transaction switch operating session</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="executeCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="c0fb6e70-e139-4f17-92a0-ce26ac57ad88">
                <documentation>Execute a task under the card transaction switch operating session</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="recordCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="9c32abc5-4274-4076-b66f-593ef71381d3">
                <documentation>Record activity details/information against the card transaction switch operating session</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="retrieveCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="548e4e23-e825-471b-a2ed-7e1b651a4951">
                <documentation>Retrieve card transaction switch operating session related reports</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="requestCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="1618ec8d-5475-455b-8079-36b8ba45b067">
                <documentation>Request a service under the card transaction switch operating session</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="notifyCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="0991ba7e-d280-4b8c-8650-208217cbe537">
                <documentation>Subscribe to card transaction switch operating session notification services</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="terminateCardTransactionSwitchOperatingSession" id="1662a2cc-ca8a-44e0-b191-7e60eea607af">
                <documentation>Terminate all or some part of the card transaction switch operating session</documentation>
              </element>
            </folder>
            <folder name="Delinquent Account Handling" id="5beceb7a-aec6-4d1e-91db-acb30bacdaf9">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Delinquent Account Handling (card)" id="2ffbbf85-0575-4501-bf56-0fd0665adfbc">
                <documentation>

Example of use:

When a Card Account is assessed to be at a high risk of default, such as a Charge Card Account with high out of pattern outstandings or a Credit Card Account with significant aged balances, attempts are made to elicit the payment of the outstanding amounts or to limit further increase in risk through optimal strategies for contacting the customer and inducing payment of the outstanding amount. The Card may continue to maintain charging privileges at this stage.

General comment:

This service domain determines and executes strategies for eliciting payment from high risk Card Accounts. These strategies may include communicating with the customer through text messages, emails or phone calls, reducing the credit line or blocking the card to prevent further increase in risk, or to cancel the card and transfer it to Card Collections.

Business Purpose
:  Handle delinquent accounts (for active cards) for follow-up of payments due through periodic review and contacts. This process ends when the card account is cancelled and is transferred to Card Collections.





Пример использования:

Когда карточный счет оценивается как подверженный высокому риску дефолта, например, счет платежной карты с высокими нестандартными показателями или счет кредитной карты со значительными устаревшими балансами, предпринимаются попытки получить оплату непогашенных сумм или ограничить дальнейшее увеличение риска с помощью оптимальных стратегий для связи с клиентом и побуждения оплаты непогашенной суммы. На этом этапе карта может продолжать поддерживать привилегии зарядки.

Общее замечание:

Этот домен услуг определяет и выполняет стратегии получения платежей с карточных счетов высокого риска. Эти стратегии могут включать в себя общение с клиентом посредством текстовых сообщений, электронных писем или телефонных звонков, уменьшение кредитной линии или блокирование карты для предотвращения дальнейшего увеличения риска или для отмены карты и передачи ее в коллекции карт.

деловая цель
: Обработка просроченных счетов (для активных карт) для отслеживания платежей, подлежащих периодическому обзору и контактам. Этот процесс заканчивается, когда карточный счет отменяется и переносится в карточные коллекции.



Service Domain - Card Delinquent Account Handling
This service domain determines and executes strategies for eliciting payment from high risk Card Accounts. These strategies may include communicating with the customer through text messages, emails or phone calls. The Card may continue to maintain charging privileges at this stage. Eventually it can be necessary to reduce the credit line or block the card to prevent further increase in risk, or to cancel the card and transfer it to Card Collections. 

Executive Summary
This service domain handles delinquent accounts (for active cards) for follow-up of payments due through periodic review and contacts. This process ends when the card account is cancelled and is transferred to Card Collections

Examples Of Use
When a Card Account is assessed to be at a high risk of default, such as a Charge Card Account with high out of pattern outstandings or a Credit Card Account with significant aged balances, attempts are made to elicit the payment of the outstanding amounts or to limit further increase in risk
</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="activateCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="8465aafc-2d8e-431a-a077-2cbd4d9e5060">
                <documentation>Assign responsibility for the card delinquent account handling procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="configureCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="83e98990-a65f-405a-b22f-00c12f4be1c8">
                <documentation>Amend the configuration arrangements/parameters governing the card delinquent account handling procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="executeCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="0a754c22-f28a-4fa2-91b4-bb4e35a2bf70">
                <documentation>Execute a task under the card delinquent account handling procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="recordCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="1a262992-dcab-41e8-8868-5be06aa6720b">
                <documentation>Record activity details/information against the card delinquent account handling procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="requestCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="ca0abc3c-f271-4cda-baaa-3855880e8209">
                <documentation> Request a service under the card delinquent account handling procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="retrieveCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="fb222420-df05-494d-a458-3a5818ee5a4d">
                <documentation>Retrieve card delinquent account handling procedure related reports</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="updateCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="ebf41354-15ea-4f49-895c-c8d2087923d4">
                <documentation>Update work tasks and activity details for the card delinquent account handling procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="notifyCardDelinquentAccountHandlingProcedure" id="39d16456-a785-4e8a-9826-b7cd376929d5">
                <documentation>Subscribe to card delinquent account handling procedure notification services</documentation>
              </element>
            </folder>
            <folder name="Card Collections" id="5d2aa76b-54ce-4f5c-be28-f79979b056c3">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Card Collections" id="1c8059a7-7d2d-47b2-8ca5-65e069e43f47">
                <documentation>Example of use:
A card account is canceled when the age of outstanding balance exceeds policy limits (normally 90 days) or when delinquency management and dunning efforts are determined to be unsuccessful at eliciting payment. The account is then assigned to an internal Collections department or an external Collection Agency for making aggressive attempts at securing the payment of the outstandings.

General comment:
This service domain handles the determination and execution of the optimal strategy to ensure the collection of unsecured distressed card debt, which may include aggressive collection efforts, renegotiation of payments terms in order to improve customer commitment to make the payment, or to take any applicable legal actions against the customer.

Business Purpose
:  Administer the recovery of outstanding amounts from cancelled card accounts through internal or external collection agencies. This may involve negotiating payment terms or interest write-down.




Пример использования:
Карточный счет аннулируется, когда возраст непогашенного остатка превышает пределы политики (обычно 90 дней) или когда управление просрочки и усилия dunning определяются как неудачные при получении платежа. Затем эта учетная запись присваивается внутреннему отделу инкассо или внешнему Агентству по инкассо для осуществления агрессивных попыток обеспечить выплату выдающихся сумм.

Общее замечание:
Данный домен услуг занимается определением и исполнением оптимальной стратегии по обеспечению взыскания необеспеченной проблемной карточной задолженности, которая может включать в себя агрессивные усилия по взысканию, пересмотр условий платежей с целью улучшения обязательств клиента по осуществлению платежа или принятие любых применимых юридических мер против клиента.

деловая цель
: Администрирование взыскании суммы задолженности отменено карточных счетов через внутренние или внешние коллекторские агентства. Это может включать согласование условий оплаты или списание процентов.


Service Domain - Card Collections
The card collection process relates to the determination and execution of the optimal strategy to ensure the collection of unsecured distressed card debt, which may include aggressive collection efforts, renegotiation of payments terms in order to improve customer commitment to make the payment, or to take any applicable legal actions against the customer.

Executive Summary
This service domain administers the recovery of outstanding amounts from cancelled card accounts through internal or external collection agencies. This may involve negotiating payment terms and/or interest write-downs.

Examples Of Use
A card account is canceled when the age of outstanding balance exceeds policy limits or when delinquency management and dunning efforts are determined to be unsuccessful at eliciting payment.It is then assigned to an agency for making aggressive attempts at securing the payment of the outstandings.</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="notifyCardCollectionsProcedure" id="a0373471-5520-4747-b629-8912fdd9fd4b">
                <documentation>Subscribe to card collections procedure notification services</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="activateCardCollectionsProcedure" id="5f23827c-29dc-4b9c-a8ad-29be6a667f4e">
                <documentation>Assign responsibility for the card collections procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="retrieveCardCollectionsProcedure" id="c29e3363-cc86-4c19-8f3c-0b57d2ccd47b">
                <documentation> Retrieve card collections procedure related reports</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="configureCardCollectionsProcedure" id="80130ef7-1f10-49a6-95dc-9cc0191d37a4">
                <documentation>Amend the configuration arrangements/parameters governing the card collections procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="executeCardCollectionsProcedure" id="2512b018-f47e-4091-b35b-3bce89357fb0">
                <documentation>Execute a task under the card collections procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="recordCardCollectionsProcedure" id="13b7fc48-9f9f-415d-b68f-ae518fc939ca">
                <documentation>Record activity details/information against the card collections procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="requestCardCollectionsProcedure" id="af5f3265-6065-4386-8b03-05bd8bd70591">
                <documentation>Request a service under the card collections procedure</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="updateCardCollectionsProcedure" id="911b8847-a572-4fde-8cb4-911dd64a3b24">
                <documentation>Update work tasks and activity details for the card collections procedure</documentation>
              </element>
            </folder>
          </folder>
          <folder name="Payments" id="5c6454e9-b589-453b-9832-ada5a0013db4">
            <folder name="Payments Execution" id="918526ef-e10f-40ee-963e-134774b583be">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Payments Execution" id="34eabdca-5f1b-43b6-92a4-8a22ae186844">
                <documentation> Example of use:

Transfer funds from a customer account with the bank to an account with another bank

General comment:

Payment Execution handles the bank side of a payment, the movement of money from debtor account to creditor account. Payments need to be authorised and validated against customer agreements, before being issued to Payment Execution. Payment Execution figures out whether debtor and creditor accounts are on-us, selecting the appropriate payment mechanism to reach these if not. It delegates the actual creation of debit and credit entries to Position Keeping.

Business Purpose
:  Orchestrate the execution of payments between accounts within the bank or with other banks, selecting the appropriate payment mechanism

Documentation
 Orchestrate the execution of payment transactions, with, and between bank using any appropriate payment mechanism (A/C, wire, ACH)





Пример использования:

Перевод средств со счета клиента в банке на счет в другом банке

Общее замечание:

Исполнение платежа обрабатывает банковскую сторону платежа, движение денег со счета должника на счет кредитора. Выплаты должны быть уполномочены и проверка договоров с клиентами, перед отправкой платежа. Выполнение платежа выясняет, находятся ли счета должника и кредитора на нас, выбирая соответствующий механизм оплаты, чтобы достичь их, если нет. Он делегирует фактическое создание дебетовых и кредитовых проводок в ведение позиции.

деловая цель
: Организовывать выполнение платежей между счетами в банке или в других банках, выбирая соответствующий механизм оплаты

Документация
 Организовывать выполнение платежных операций, с и между банком, используя любой соответствующий механизм оплаты (A/C, wire, ACH)


Service Domain - Payment Execution
Payment Execution handles the back-end processing of a movement funds from a debtor account to a creditor account. Payments need to have been authorized and validated against customer/bank agreements before being instructed to Payment Execution. Payment Execution then determines whether debtor and creditor accounts are held within the bank and if not selects the appropriate payment mechanism/channel to use to complete the transfer. It is responsible for ensuring that both (or neither) sides of the exchange are completed successfully

Executive Summary
This service domains processes the movement of funds between accounts within the bank or to/from an account held with another bank, selecting the appropriate payment mechanism

Examples Of Use
Funds are transferred from a customer's account with the bank to a payee account held at another bank
</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="initiatePaymentExecutionTransaction" id="119ed2fd-468b-4530-a2cc-05ea99a02533">
                <documentation>Initiate a payment execution transaction</documentation>
              </element>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="executePaymentExecutionTransaction" id="27976748-f58e-4ffc-8207-8d0b1b5b2e0d">
