          <folder name="Fraud/AML Resolution" id="f6995da4-64ea-40f9-a6bf-e9ccd92ffcb7">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Fraud/AML Resolution" id="af32a2b6-e662-4c06-b466-30c1d8d8aab6">
              <documentation>Example of use:

A pattern of possible fraud is highlighted in transaction records that is researched and evidence of fraud discovered. Prosecution is initiated

General comment:

This service domain handles the resolution of detected fraud and AML issues in production. Typically a specialist team that handles each case as a project with a structured procedure for analysis and resolution tasks

Business Purpose
:  Review, diagnose and respond to detected production activity that has been identified as potential fraud/AML behavior





Пример использования:

В отчетах о сделках, которые изучаются и обнаруживаются доказательства мошенничества, указывается на характер возможного мошенничества. Возбуждено уголовное преследование 

Общее замечание:

Этот домен обслуживания обрабатывает разрешение обнаруженных проблем мошенничества и AML в производстве. Как правило, команда специалистов, которая обрабатывает каждый случай как проект со структурированной процедурой анализа и решения задач

деловая цель
: Анализ, диагностика и реагирование на обнаруженную производственную деятельность, которая была определена как потенциальное мошенничество

Service Domain - Fraud AML Resolution
This service domain handles the diagnosis/confirmation of detected potential fraud and AML issues in production. Typically the service is supported with specialist teams to  handle cases with structured procedures and techniques for analysis and undertaking the required resolution/escalation tasks.

Detailed Summary
This service domain reviews, diagnoses and responds to potential fraud/AML behavior that has been detected during production processing.

Executive Summary
This service domain reviews, diagnoses and responds to potential fraud/AML behavior that has been detected during production processing

Examples Of Use
A pattern of possible fraud is highlighted in transaction records that is researched and evidence of fraud discovered. Prosecution/resolution activity is initiated.

</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="activateFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="b295df7f-c9c7-4189-8aaa-7e10bb6c565b">
              <documentation>Assign responsibility for the Fraud/AML Resolution Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="configureFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="53af3ec3-382a-4476-a9ab-e027e260b124">
              <documentation>Amend the configuration arrangements/parameters governing the Fraud/AML Resolution Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name=" executeFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="478d824e-e287-483b-82f3-41928fa64589">
              <documentation> Execute an automated action against an active Fraud/AML case</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="recordFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="f4825fd0-1224-45c8-a28e-3912e3071c05">
              <documentation>Record information against an active Fraud/AML case</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="updateFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="3d122482-fafe-4011-ac67-0776d3c53ea2">
              <documentation>Update details of an active Fraud/AML case</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name=" requestFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="b85887c4-a3ad-4809-8994-421a7bd08d31">
              <documentation> Request a workstep against an active Fraud/AML case</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="retrieveFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="c0ee2b5c-7eb3-4808-b3e7-fb85a8da606c">
              <documentation>Retrieve Fraud/AML case report</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name=" notifyFraud/AMLResolutionProcedure" id="7d75794d-3a5b-4041-93f3-1080507e7bfa">
              <documentation>Subscribe to Fraud/AML Resolution Procedure notification services</documentation>
            </element>
          </folder>
          <folder name="Financial Accounting" id="50590af6-7717-4daf-9841-f97966bdae38">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Financial Accounting" id="86b4ff16-8495-4603-9401-eba6d73342b2">
              <documentation>Example of use:

The corporate financial reports are assembled to schedule for accounting and general reporting needs

General comment:

This service domain handles the posting of business activity to the bank's financial accounts. These will typically be double entry ledgers and can include multiple levels of consolidation (sub-ledgers) The financial accounts conform to chart of accounts and appropriate GAP rules and are rolled up into the GL as part of the financial statements

Business Purpose
:  Financial booking of all business activity in an ledger/sub-ledger accounting structure/hierarchy according to the appropriate chart of accounts





Пример использования:

Корпоративные финансовые отчеты собираются в соответствии с графиком для нужд бухгалтерского учета и общей отчетности

Общее замечание:

Этот домен услуг обрабатывает учет деловой активности на финансовых счетах банка. Как правило, это регистры двойной записи, они могут включать несколько уровней консолидации (субкниги). финансовые счета соответствуют плану счетов и соответствующим правилам разрыва и сворачиваются в ГК как часть финансовых отчетов

деловая цель
_Бух_проводки_ всей бизнес_деятельности в структуре/иерархии бухгалтерской книги/субкниги согласно соответствующему плану счетов


Financial Accounting
This service domain handles the posting of business activity to the bank's financial accounts. These will typically be double entry ledgers and can include multiple levels of consolidation (sub-ledgers) The financial accounts conform to the bank's chart of accounts and appropriate GAP rules and are rolled up into the GL as part of the financial statements

Detailed Summary
This service domain handles financial booking of all business activity in a ledger/sub-ledger accounting structure/hierarchy according to the appropriate chart of accounts


Executive Summary
This service domain handles financial booking of all business activity in a ledger/sub-ledger accounting structure/hierarchy according to the appropriate chart of accounts

Examples Of Use
A business unit posts its financial transactions to the sub ledger at the end of the working day
</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name=" activateFinancialBookingLog" id="818c2123-93f3-4026-a01a-c9bac18ec387">
              <documentation>Assign responsibility for the Financial Booking Account/Log</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="configureFinancialBookingLog" id="4ab495f9-2318-4728-b817-7e5a10d88326">
              <documentation>Amend the configuration arrangements/parameters governing the Financial Booking Account/Log</documentation>
