          <folder name="Account Recovery" id="e390dfda-56a8-4609-a2f2-0ec1a1a0cf55">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Account Recovery" id="1ed107eb-1b9e-4c10-b72c-6cde7579c648">
              <documentation>Example of use:

A non-performing customer account is handed over for recovery after the normal relationship management efforts have failed. Additional authority is provided to renegotiate/structure the account to enable the customer to attempt recovery. This restructuring can result in write downs that need to be booked appropriately

General comment:

Handles the recovery of distressed accounts that have exceeded standard late/payment handling but have not yet been fully written off and passed to collections. The restructuring can involve partial write downs and leveraging any tax or other program of assistance that can be applied. The situation is managed until the account is recovered or a decision made to pass the account over to collections

Business Purpose
:  Handle recovery for a customer account where the standard recovery arrangements have been exhausted and a recovery plan is needed, which can include some degree of principal right-down and repayment restructuring





Пример использования:

Неработающая учетная запись клиента передается для восстановления после того, как обычные усилия по управлению отношениями потерпели неудачу. Дополнительные полномочия предоставляются пересмотреть / структурировать учетную запись, чтобы позволить клиенту попытаться восстановления. Такая реструктуризация может привести к списанию, которое необходимо забронировать надлежащим образом

Общее замечание:

Обрабатывает восстановление проблемных счетов, которые превысили стандартную обработку просроченных платежей, но еще не были полностью списаны и переданы в _коллекшен_. Реструктуризация может включать частичное списание и использование любых налогов или других программ помощи, которые могут быть применены. Ситуация управляется до восстановления учетной записи или принятия решения о передаче учетной записи в _коллекшен_

деловая цель
: Обработка восстановления для клиентского счета, где стандартные механизмы восстановления были исчерпаны и необходим план восстановления, который может включать некоторую степень основного права вниз и реструктуризации погашения




Service Domain - Account Recovery
Handles the recovery of distressed accounts that have exceeded standard late/payment handling but have not yet been fully written off and passed to collections. The restructuring can involve partial write downs and leveraging any tax or other program of assistance that can be applied. The situation is managed until the account is recovered or a decision made to pass the account over to collections

Executive Summary
This service domain handles the restructuring of a distressed account (loan) after standard recovery procedures have been exhausted

Examples Of Use
Non-performing customer account is handed over for recovery after the normal relationship management efforts have failed. Additional authority is provided to renegotiate/structure the account to enable the customer to attempt recovery. It can result in write downs that need to be booked appropriatly

</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="activateAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="27022608-3309-465e-b54c-4cb337c6f7cd">
              <documentation>Assign responsibility for the Account Recovery Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="configureAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="7a265b24-0cee-41af-8743-c3a5d1748884">
              <documentation>Comment:

Amend the configuration arrangements/parameters governing the Account Recovery Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="executeAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="64e21148-6753-41f6-9dc6-69d4ae278227">
              <documentation>Execute a task under the Account Recovery Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="recordAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="d7b64bb5-ae76-4579-8f6f-3c5c22b40991">
              <documentation>Record activity details/information against the Account Recovery Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="requestAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="67aa9eb7-7af4-4693-834c-a27e515574f7">
              <documentation>Request a service under the Account Recovery Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="retrieveAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="f4c44417-8c4e-4bd9-ad82-ac065ecf11f4">
              <documentation>Retrieve Account Recovery Procedure related reports</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="updateAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="f56748b8-41a7-409d-904c-be3218c4a44f">
              <documentation>Comment:

Update work tasks and activity details for the Account Recovery Procedure</documentation>
            </element>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="notifyAccountRecoveryProcedure" id="56020a49-3060-4e92-a143-4a091f387606">
              <documentation>Subscribe to Account Recovery Procedure notification services</documentation>
            </element>
          </folder>
          <folder name="Customer Event History" id="034fad9b-351b-400e-a207-f9823526df6b">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Customer Event History" id="156bf99a-36a3-442b-a256-b392d56c7128">
              <documentation>Example of use:

A customer contacts the call center to enquire about account transactions and during the dialogue the CSR captures a life event (e.g. the customer is moving house). The contact details and life event are captured in the customer history

General comment:

The service domain captures a wide range of customer events to build a comprehensive history of customer activity that can support subsequent behavioral analysis. This includes key sales/proposal events, relationship management events, product delivery events, detected customer triggers (typically gleaned during servicing dialogues) and possibly externally sourced customer activity. The assembled data is made available for behavioral analysis and for more general reference (as might be used for relationship management for example). Note servicing activity for root cause analysis is captured elsewhere

Business Purpose
:  Capture, classify and store relationship, servicing and product related customer events. In addition to transactional details, the log can capture life/relationship events









Пример использования:

Клиент связывается с колл-центром, чтобы узнать о транзакциях по счету, и во время диалога CSR фиксирует событие жизни (например, клиент перемещает дом). Контактные данные и события фиксируются в истории клиента 

Общее замечание:

Домен обслуживания фиксирует широкий спектр событий клиента для построения полной истории активности клиента, которая может поддерживать последующий анализ поведения. Это включает в себя ключевые события продаж / предложения, события управления отношениями, события доставки продукта, обнаруженные триггеры клиентов (обычно получаемые во время диалогов обслуживания) и, возможно, внешнюю активность клиентов. Собранные данные доступны для поведенческого анализа и для более общего использования (например, для управления отношениями). Примечание действия по обслуживанию для анализа причин фиксируется в другом месте

деловая цель
: Захват, классифицировать и хранить отношения, обслуживание и связанные с продуктом события клиентов. В дополнение к транзакционным деталям, журнал может фиксировать события жизни / отношений



Service Domain - Customer Event History
The service domain captures a wide range of customer events to build a comprehensive history of customer activity that can support subsequent behavioral analysis. This includes key sales/proposal events, relationship management events, product delivery events, detected customer triggers (typically gleaned during servicing dialogues) and possibly externally sourced customer activity. The assembled data is made available for behavioral analysis and for more general reference (as might be used for relationship management for example).

Detailed Summary
This service domain captures, classifies and stores relationship, servicing and product fulfillment related customer events. In addition to servicing and product transaction details, the log can capture life/relationship events that are revealed during customer exchanges.

Executive Summary
This service domain captures, classifies and stores relationship, servicing and product fulfillment related customer events. In addition to servicing and product transaction details, the log can capture life/relationship events that are revealed during customer exchanges.

Examples Of Use
A customer contacts the call center to enquire about account transactions and during the dialogue the servicing representative detects a life event (e.g. the customer is moving house). The contact details and life event are captured in the customer history.

</documentation>
            </element>
