</documentation>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Administer" id="3aef6c58-8474-4fe0-8bd7-164a60403ae2">
        <documentation>Handle and assign the day to day activities, capture time, costs and income for an operational unit. 
Example: Administer the time reporting and billing for the specialist sales support team. 

Unassigned
Administration-allocated
Under-administration
Administered-under-review
Administration-suspended
Administration-concluded

</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Direct" id="7ab9f909-9cc8-4d6d-8d05-aa7f2be9fee6">
        <documentation>Define the policies, goals &amp; objectives and strategies for an organizational entity or unit. 
Example: Direct a division of the enterprise.

Unassigned
Assigned-strategy-pending
Strategy-in-force
Strategy-under-review
Strategy-suspended
Strategy-concluded
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Manage" id="cc5cc0ab-aa3f-41de-9722-ceed9a3f03b7">
        <documentation>Oversee the working of a business unit, assign work, manage against a plan and troubleshoot issues. 
Example: Manage the day to day activities at a bank branch location.

Unassigned
Assigned-plan-pending
Under-management
Managed-under-review
Management-suspended
Management-concluded</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Operate" id="9bad1796-cb5d-4260-ad2b-fd1bed350413">
        <documentation>Operate equipment and/or a largely automated facility. 
Example: Operate the bank's internal intranet facility.

Inactive
In-operation
In-operation-qualified
Operating-suspended
Operation-concluded</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Process" id="4c0cef07-09c2-4e4e-9123-e9834590eafe">
        <documentation>Complete work tasks following a defined procedure in support of general office activities and product and service delivery. 
Example: Process the evaluation and completion of customer offers.

Inactive
In-processing
In-processing-qualified
Processing-suspended
Processing-concluded
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Assess" id="75b7463f-2d02-4709-a15c-d325013dd444">
        <documentation>To test or assess an entity, possibly against some formal qualification or certification requirement. 
Examples: Perform regulatory tests on a proposed financial transaction and check a new offer conforms to an existing contractual agreement.

In-use
In-use-assessment-pending
Assessment-ongoing
Assessment-failed-suspended
Assessment-failed-in-use
Assessment-passed
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Design" id="7a929ae8-2ca1-491f-be63-e1d44180cb03">
        <documentation>Create and maintain a design for a procedure, product/service model or other such entity. 
Example: Create and maintain product designs and analytical models.

Design registered
Design-pending
Design-in-force
Design-under-review
Design-active-suspended
Design-inactive-suspended
Design-expired</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Develop" id="ac231806-9799-4de1-aca8-52307fec9236">
        <documentation>To build or enhance something, typically an IT production systems. Includes development, Assessment and deployment activities. 
Example: Build, enhance, test and deploy a major enhancement to a production product processing system.

Dev-required-in-use
Suspended-requiring-dev
Under-development
Pending-acceptance
Pending-deployment
Development-concluded-in-use

</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Maintain" id="57891770-86ed-4b80-9b8b-370276761743">
        <documentation>Provide a maintenance service and repair devices/equipment as necessary. 
Example: Establish a maintenance and repair program covering the PC technology used in the central offices.

Inactive
Maintenance-service-active
Maint-pending-in-use
Maint-pending-inactive
Under-repair
Repair-completed-in-use
Maintenance-service-concluded
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Register" id="306f199b-def9-4c47-a7b3-5f1d7d75f6b7">
        <documentation>Capture and maintain reference information about some type of entity. 
Example: Register customer reference details in a directory.

Inactive
Directory-active
Directory -active-item-current
Directory-suspended
Directory-expired</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Enroll" id="dc94dd55-bef1-4832-8912-9cf4bc24d3f0">
        <documentation>Maintain a membership for some group or related collection of parties. 
Example: Administer the memebrship status of a syndicate of investors.

Inactive
Active-enrollment
Active-enrollment-suspended
Enrollment-service-concluded
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Allocate" id="4894a1a1-5bc6-4a18-8b7b-561a9df626d1">
        <documentation>Maintain an inventory or holding of some resource and make assignments/allocations as requested. 
Example: Track the inventory and administer the distribution of central cash holdings throughout the branch &amp; ATM network.

Inactive
Resource-pool-active-available
Resources-fully-assigned,
Resources-revocated
Resources-pool-service-concluded</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Agree Terms" id="9fb1ccb3-5475-46e8-a92c-d8cac29bcbd7">
        <documentation>Maintain the terms and conditions that apply to a commercial relationship. 
Example: Define and maintain the terms govering the contratcual relationship with a customer.

No-agreement
Agreement-pending
Agreement-in-force
Agreement-update-pending
Agreement-expired</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Transact" id="2283edda-62f1-43fc-ac52-b769875e0e88">
        <documentation>Execute a well-bounded financial transaction/task, typically involving largely automated/structured fulfillment processing. 
Example: Execute a payment transaction.

Execution-ongoing
Execution-qualified
Execution-suspended
Execution-concluded</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Fulfill" id="c469cdec-12cf-42d3-aeae-5b72db190127">
        <documentation>Fulfill any scheduled and ad-hoc obligations under a service arrangement, most typically for a financial product or facility. 
Example: Perform the scheduled (e.g. statements, standing orders) and ad-hoc/requested (e.g. balance inquiries, fund transfers) fulfillment tasks for a customer current account facility.

Inactive
Fulfillment-services-active
Fulfillment-active-qualified
Fulfillment-suspende
Fulfillment-concluded</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Track" id="6283009b-148d-4752-936f-1ff63f4d9080">
        <documentation>Maintain a log of transactions or activity, typically a financial account/journal or a log of activity to support analysis. Examples: Maintain a financial journal of transactions processed for a product or service and maintain a log of customer events and activity for subsequent analysis.

Inactive
Tracking-active
Tracking-suspended
Tracking-under-anaysis
Tracking-expired</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Monitor" id="81326583-ceea-4b60-b2f6-aaa181eeed0c">
        <documentation>Monitor and define the status/rating of some entity. 
Examples: Monitor the status and key indicators of a customer to influence on-line interactions and track the status of issued cards for security and access control.

Inactive
Monitoring-active
Monitoring-update-pending
Monitoring-concluded
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="=Analyze" id="e567da1d-2d4b-4bce-b4e2-1600960a0389">
        <documentation>Analyze the performance or behavior of some on-going activity or entity. 
Examples: Provide behavioral insights and analysis into customer behavior and analyze financial market activity in order to identify opportunities, define pricing and evaluate risks.

Inactive
Analysis-active
Analysis-update-pending
Analysis-concluded
</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Action Term" id="b9fe7fb8-85fe-4615-90dc-55e872de9ec8">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Initiate" id="f38dc250-e37a-4283-b7c9-d0e5e556147c">
        <documentation>Begin an action including any required initialization. 
Example: Initiate a payment transaction.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Evaluate" id="8f2c682b-01d3-43cc-ab7e-51915a17829f">
        <documentation>Perform a check, trial or evaluation. 
Example: The eligibility to sell a product is checked against an existing agreement.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Request" id="dc1937e1-cbb7-4ee2-af0d-588b5b50dfce">
        <documentation>Request for the provision of some service. 
Example: A customer requests that a standing order is set up on the current account.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Record" id="d16df00e-b304-4985-89a9-8fc78508d6d6">
        <documentation>Capture transaction or event detail associated with a life cycle step . 
Example: An employee logs time spent working on a project against the plan.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Authorize" id="959bf207-72df-41c6-b3ff-c9f35b901103">
        <documentation>Allow the execution of a transaction. 
Example: Regulatory compliance authorizes a product design feature.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Activate" id="9ab2b4c4-2e1f-43ba-8057-9aa1008f6ad3">
        <documentation>Commence/open an operational or administrative service. 
Example: Activate the ATM network operation.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Configure" id="7097c383-2e3b-4315-8cb2-f86e18f41458">
        <documentation>Change the operating parameters for an ongoing service/capability. 
Example: Change on-line ATMs in the network to take machines out of service.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Create" id="a8da5da7-00d1-4ef3-84b3-8553d73150cf">
        <documentation> Manufacture and distribute an item (terms considered: create/manufacture/make). 
Example: Create a new analytical model design.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Register" id="28bbdb75-e77a-4cc5-9cd6-9d6f0a5601b0">
        <documentation>Record the details of a newly identified entity. 
Example: Capture a new customer's details.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Update" id="a5ac3d2a-7b10-43fe-aa82-978274d7afbf">
        <documentation>Change the value of some control record instance's properties. 
Example: Update a customer's reference details with a change of address.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Provide" id="f17a003e-73f0-414a-86e1-fe35abc2a4f1">
        <documentation>Assign or allocate resources or facilities. 
Example: A branch requests an allocation of cash for its tellers.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Execute" id="d986b9fc-2e8b-4cd9-80e8-e7588090a116">
        <documentation>Execute a task or action on an established facility (note typically creates a result). 
Example: Apply a payment to a charge card.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Terminate" id="77395858-2e3d-4dd7-bc9c-7e4ddc820915">
        <documentation>Conclude, complete, activity. 
Example: Terminate the use of a product version.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Retrieve" id="79ef5d60-cda0-4f83-93f1-29ba70ce6dcd">
        <documentation>Return information/report as requested. 
Examples: Obtain an account balance. Request a report covering activity analysis.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="->Notify" id="79ca1b17-0c33-4390-bee4-adee08707d77">
        <documentation>Provide details against a predefined notification agreement. 
Example: A unit subscribes to update notifications from the customer agreement service domain.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
